  "prefLabel": "Ed 1401.02 Scope",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1401.02 Scope.\n\n(a) These rules shall apply to any for-profit or non-profit entity applying to offer an educational program, consistent with these rules, that meets the minimum standards for approval to grant credit leading to graduation.\n\n(b) These rules shall apply to students, emancipated minors, or students with disabilities in accordance with their individualized education program (IEP) as determined by the IEP team.\n\n(c) Successful completion of approved learn everywhere programs shall result in a certificate award by the learn everywhere program redeemable for high school credit leading to graduation in the approved subject matter pursuant to Ed 306.23(g) table 306-1.\n\n(d) These rules shall apply to all school districts, chartered public schools, public academies, or local education agencies (LEAs).\n\nSource. #13090, eff 8-14-20 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Ed 1400); ss by #13393, eff 6-10-22; ss by #13924, eff 4-12-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1400.html"
